php-proj for Debian
====================

This package provides PHP bindings for the PROJ cartographic projections library.

Installation
------------

After installing this package, the extension will be automatically enabled for
all PHP SAPIs (CLI, FPM, Apache, etc.) using the phpenmod mechanism.

You can verify the extension is loaded with:
    php -m | grep proj

Configuration
-------------

The extension is configured via the standard PHP module configuration system.
The configuration file is located at:
    /etc/php/*/mods-available/proj.ini

To manually enable/disable the extension:
    phpenmod proj    # Enable
    phpdismod proj   # Disable

For specific SAPI or PHP version:
    phpenmod -s cli proj           # Enable for CLI only
    phpenmod -v 8.1 proj           # Enable for PHP 8.1 only
    phpenmod -v 8.1 -s fpm proj    # Enable for PHP 8.1 FPM only

Requirements
------------

This extension requires:
- libproj22 (>= 6.0.0) - The PROJ cartographic projections library
- PHP 7.4 or later

Development
-----------

Development headers are provided in the php-proj-dev package, which includes:
- Header files for extension development
- Documentation for the C API

Troubleshooting
--------------

If the extension fails to load, check:

1. PHP error logs for specific error messages
2. Ensure libproj is properly installed:
    dpkg -l libproj22

3. Verify the extension file exists:
    find /usr/lib/php -name "proj.so"

4. Check PHP module configuration:
    php --ini | grep proj

5. Test with a simple script:
    php -r "var_dump(extension_loaded('proj'));"

For more information, see:
- PROJ library documentation: https://proj.org/
- Extension source code and examples in /usr/share/doc/php-proj/

Bug Reports
-----------

Please report bugs to the package maintainer or upstream project.
Include PHP version, PROJ version, and a minimal reproduction case.

